{"name":"Mystical Shade","hex":"#4c5364","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mystical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to mystics or mysticism.","Having a spiritual or magical significance that transcends human understanding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystical"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shade (character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Shade is a comic book character developed in the 1940s for National Comics, first appearing in the pages of Flash Comics in a story titled \"The Man Who Commanded the Night\", scripted by Gardner Fox and illustrated by Hal Sharp. Debuting as a villain, the Shade was best known for fighting against two generations of superheroes, most notably the Golden Age and Silver Age versions of the Flash. He eventually became a mentor for Jack Knight, the son of the Golden Age Starman, Ted Knight, a hero the Shade had also fought."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Shade_%28DC_Comics_character%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shade_(character)"},{"title":"Mysticism","blocks":[{"text":"Mysticism encompasses religious traditions of human transformation aided by various practices and religious experiences. Popularly, mysticism is used synonymously with mystical experience, a neologism which refers to an ecstatic unitive experience of becoming one with God, the Absolute, or all that exists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Hildegard_von_Bingen_Liber_Divinorum_Operum.jpg/330px-Hildegard_von_Bingen_Liber_Divinorum_Operum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mysticism"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg/500px-Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg/500px-Peter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Appearance of the Holy Spirit before Saint Teresa of Ávila, Peter Paul Rubens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeter_Paul_Rubens_166.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/500px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/1280px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Khagdaev1.JPG/500px-Khagdaev1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Buryat shaman performing a ritual on Olkhon Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKhagdaev1.J